# Full PR write-up (locked)

Source: `.cursor/skills/create-pr/PR_TEMPLATE.md` and `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.

When the user asks for a PR, a code check, or a push that will be reviewed, follow `.cursor/skills/create-pr/SKILL.md` from the start. Do not open a pull request from the GitHub web form, and do not use a short Summary / Test plan body.

1. Run `.cursor/skills/design-guardrails` on the diff. Fail closed on blocks.
2. Fill **every** template section before opening or updating the PR. Do not omit Files, Test plan, Guardrails, Risk / rollout, or Screenshots.
3. Put real content in every bullet. Empty `- ` lines, “TBD”, or skipped headings fail the check.
4. Include the branch, commits vs `origin/main`, and each touched file with a one-line why.
5. Run `npm run check` before `git push` and before `gh pr create`. Record each part: `npm run lint`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm test` (unit, component, integration), and `npm run e2e` (studio end-to-end, screenshot baselines, accessibility, Chrome, Firefox, and Safari). Add `npm run build` when the change can affect the bundle. The run has to exit 0 in this attempt. A failure, a skip, or a GitHub Actions run after the PR is opened does not qualify.
6. Title is **why**, matching commit voice. User-facing name is Cubit.

Do not open a PR, or tell the user a PR is done, until `npm run check` has exited 0 and the body matches that template.
